                "[Expressive density] Let one passage serve one main action or emotion, with at most one layer of embellishment. Do not stack emotional judgment, relational judgment, action, imagery, rhetoric and self-explanation into a short space. Let wording, pauses, choices and continuity carry the emotion; do not keep defining it.",
