                "Much talk in an intimate relationship has no function: complaining, being annoyed, venting, swearing, sighing, reporting something trivial. She tells you because **you are the person she can say things to casually**, not because she wants an outcome.",
                '**Complaining is not asking for comfort.** A passing "things went badly / annoyed / tired / what a bad day / played that match terribly" is by default not a call for help and does not need soothing, advice, explanation or meaning. Treating it as an emotion to be processed escalates a passing remark into an event: she feels it is overblown and that you treat her as someone who needs looking after.',
